    {
     "type": "h",
     "html": "Independent 1: parking fees"
    },
    {
     "type": "write",
     "id": "ws-intro-fee",
     "mode": "independent",
     "title": "Parking fees",
     "goal": "Create <code>ParkingFee.java</code> with <code>public static int fee(int hours)</code>. The first hour is free, each hour after that costs $2, and nobody pays more than $10. In <code>main</code>, print the fee for 1, 3 and 8 hours.",
     "requirements": [
      "<code>fee</code> returns the amount; <code>main</code> prints it",
      "Zero hours costs $0, not a negative amount"
     ],
     "files": [
      "ParkingFee.java"
     ],
     "starter": [],
     "tests": [
      [
       "CheckParkingFee.java",
       "public class CheckParkingFee {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(\"fee(0) = \" + ParkingFee.fee(0));\n        System.out.println(\"fee(2) = \" + ParkingFee.fee(2));\n        System.out.println(\"fee(6) = \" + ParkingFee.fee(6));\n        System.out.println(\"fee(7) = \" + ParkingFee.fee(7));\n    }\n}\n"
      ]
     ],
     "testsRun": "CheckParkingFee",
     "hints": [
      "Handle the free case first: if <code>hours &lt;= 1</code>, return 0.",
      "Otherwise the cost is <code>(hours - 1) * 2</code>. If that's more than 10, return 10."
     ],
     "checks": [],
     "run": "ParkingFee",
     "output": "1 hours: $0\n3 hours: $4\n8 hours: $10",
     "testsOutput": "fee(0) = 0\nfee(2) = 2\nfee(6) = 10\nfee(7) = 10",
     "solution": [
      [
       "ParkingFee.java",
       "public class ParkingFee {\n    public static int fee(int hours) {\n        if (hours <= 1) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        int cost = (hours - 1) * 2;\n        if (cost > 10) {\n            return 10;\n        }\n        return cost;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(\"1 hours: $\" + fee(1));\n        System.out.println(\"3 hours: $\" + fee(3));\n        System.out.println(\"8 hours: $\" + fee(8));\n    }\n}\n"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h",
     "html": "Independent 2: a counting game"
    },
    {
     "type": "write",
     "id": "ws-intro-counting",
     "mode": "independent",
     "title": "A counting game",
     "goal": "Create <code>CountingGame.java</code> that prints the numbers 1 to 15, one per line. Replace multiples of 3 with <code>Fizz</code>, multiples of 5 with <code>Buzz</code>, and multiples of both with <code>FizzBuzz</code>.",
     "requirements": [
      "One loop",
      "An <code>if</code> / <code>else if</code> chain that checks the \"both\" case first"
     ],
     "files": [
      "CountingGame.java"
     ],
     "starter": [],
     "tests": [],
     "testsRun": null,
     "hints": [
      "Why check \"both\" first? 15 is a multiple of 3, so a <code>% 3</code> check that comes first would catch it and print only <code>Fizz</code>.",
      "Multiples of both 3 and 5 are the multiples of 15: <code>i % 15 == 0</code>."
     ],
     "checks": [
      {
       "pattern": "\\b(for|while)\\s*\\(",
       "message": "Use a loop.",
       "file": null
      }
     ],
     "run": "CountingGame",
     "output": "1\n2\nFizz\n4\nBuzz\nFizz\n7\n8\nFizz\nBuzz\n11\nFizz\n13\n14\nFizzBuzz",
     "testsOutput": null,
     "solution": [
      [
       "CountingGame.java",
       "public class CountingGame {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 15; i++) {\n            if (i % 15 == 0) {\n                System.out.println(\"FizzBuzz\");\n            } else if (i % 3 == 0) {\n                System.out.println(\"Fizz\");\n            } else if (i % 5 == 0) {\n                System.out.println(\"Buzz\");\n            } else {\n                System.out.println(i);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n"
      ]
     ]
    }
