     "type": "p",
     "html": "Java evaluates the operands of <code>+</code> and <code>-</code> from left to right. In <code>s.pop() - s.pop()</code>, the left <code>pop</code> runs first and gets the top value; the right one gets the value that was underneath. That order matters for <code>-</code> and <code>/</code>, where swapping the operands changes the answer."
